expires 2026-09-20.  **THE DEFECT IS REAL AND THE GATE'S OWN COMMENT ALREADY STATES IT**, which is the 
structure-knew-and-the-record-did-not shape with the halves swapped -- here the tool was articulate and the ledger row 
was empty:  *\"ieee_store carries a far-future date because GATE 3 covers it -- against TOTAL comparator death only, 
and by the vacuity-prone `grep -c PASS == 0` form this helper was written to avoid, so it is a weaker exemption than 
it looks.\"*  So the warrant for the exemption is a control that (a) detects only TOTAL death of the comparator, not a 
wrong ANSWER from it, and (b) is written in the exact vacuity-prone form the selfmutant helper exists to replace.  **A 
2099 date means no calendar will ever surface this**, unlike the eight dated exemptions `wiringcliff` records as 
expiring together on 2026-09-20.  **THE UPGRADE THE ROW NAMES IS THEREFORE: give `ieee_store` a real `selfmutant_one` 
call and move it from `SM_EXEMPT` to `SM_COVERED`.**  Note the gate ALREADY defends that move against paper progress 
-- a later check requires every `SM_COVERED` stem to have a real `selfmutant_one` call, added after a pass-2 seat 
measured BOTH cheats green (delete the call and keep the name -> GREEN; move a stem to COVERED and write no mutant -> 
