     "title": "check_probe_wiring.py's EXEMPT table expires as a block and the checker then hard-fails -- and NOT ONE 
of the entries is a cheap wiring: every reason string names a prerequisite that does not exist.  DERIVE the population 
and the date, never quote them: `grep -n 2026-09-20 tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py' for the set (the file states 
the count in its own comment), and the comparison is `d < today' so the block is still VALID on its stamped date and 
first reds the day after.  (SUPERSEDED TITLE, kept only as the demoted record of what was claimed: \"EIGHT 
probe-wiring exemptions expire on 2026-09-20 together and the checker hard-fails -- four are cheap, only four need a 
design round\".  Wrong on the count, wrong on the date by one in the safe direction, and wrong that any are cheap; its 
own halves did not add up against the population.)",
     "state": "in work",
