independently reproducing \"exactly six problems\".\nI did run it, and got six.  Its timings are source-based 
estimates and are NOT measured runs -- so\nthe cost side of \"four are cheap\" remains an estimate, and the row should 
not repeat it as measured.***  *** MEASURED 2026-09-17 BY THE OPUS 5 SEAT, ON A BATCH THAT WAS NOT ASKED ABOUT WIRING 
-- AND IT IS THE SHARPEST ANSWER IN THAT BATCH TO \"what is the smallest edit that breaks the fix and still passes?\" 
