emitted code on\nevery compiler this project targets is what was already intended**, which is why the severity is 
LOW\neven though the language calls it undefined.\n\n*** THE TEST-FIRST ORDER IS ALREADY SATISFIED, WHICH IS UNUSUAL 
AND WORTH NOTING. ***  The witness\nexists and is RED on the committed build: running `regress/lca_confbus_probe.py` 
against\n`build-asan/gxemul` emits\n\n    dev_lca.c:125:21: runtime error: left shift of 2048 by 20 places cannot be\n 
                     represented in type 'int'\n\nSo the reproduce-before-you-edit step is DONE and 
preserved\n(`regress/artifacts/lcashiftub/ubsan_HEAD_20260907.raw`).  The post-fix half is: the same command,\nsame 
binary path, and **the diagnostic must be ABSENT**.  Same script, opposite outcome -- which is\nthe ladder's clause 
(i) exactly.\n\n**WHAT THE ROUND OWES, and the one real decision in it:**\n\nThe two-direction control above is a 
UBSAN DIFFERENTIAL, and this project has that filed as its own\nround ([[ubsanshiftlane]]) because it is a NEW 
MEASUREMENT LANE -- a second binary and a STDERR\noracle rather than a value oracle.  **So the honest choice 
is:**\n\n* **(a) ship the fix with the UBSAN differential as its detector**, which means building at least a\n  
minimal version of the lane in this round -- and a lane added inside a fix round is a lane nobody\n  reviewed, which 
is the exact objection `ubsanshiftlane` was filed to avoid; or\n* **(b) ship the fix with a SOURCE PIN** -- a check 
asserting the expression is `0x800U` -- and\n  leave the differential to its own round.  `#510`'s own product comments 
already name a source pin\n  as the legitimate alternative to UBSAN for precisely this class (\"No row can kill a `1U' 
-> `1'\n  regression; UBSAN or a source pin can\").\n\n**(b) is in scope and (a) is not**, on this project's own 
stopping rule: the fix is a one-token\ncorrectness repair, and expanding it into a new measurement lane is the scope 
creep the rule exists\nto refuse.  *Recorded as a reasoned choice rather than a preference, so a reviewer can disagree 
with\nthe reason.*\n\n**COST: a build.**  The edit must propagate to all four trees and `build-asan` must be REBUILT 
for\nthe post-fix measurement, which is the only expensive part and is why this was not executed the\nmoment it was 
designed -- a rebuild must not overlap a running seat.\n\n**AND THE POST-FIX RUN IS THE ONE THAT MATTERS MORE THAN THE 
FIX.**  If the diagnostic does NOT\ndisappear, the repair is wrong or the site is not the one being reported, and that 
is a finding\nabout the measurement rather than a formality.  Predict-then-measure: it should vanish, and 
nothing\nelse in the probe's four rows should move (3/4 before, 3/4 after -- the `bus kill` row is a\ndifferent defect 
and stays RED).\n\n*** FIXED AND MEASURED IN BOTH DIRECTIONS, 2026-09-07, as `#511`. ***\n\n    HEAD    1 diagnostic   
  ubsan_HEAD_20260907.raw\n    FIXED   0 diagnostics    ubsan_FIXED_20260907.raw\n    control  build/ scores 3/4 
before AND after, same three rows green, `bus kill' still RED\n             (a different defect) -- NOTHING ELSE 
MOVED\n\n**The pre-registered prediction held exactly**: the diagnostic vanished and no other row moved.  All\nfour 
trees cleared two-part after the propagate (`est/`: source tree, part 2 N/A).\n\n**The detector is the differential 
itself and it is NOT GATE-WIRED**, which the CHANGELOG block says\nin those words.  A source pin was considered and 
rejected: it would test the TEXT while this round\nhas the BEHAVIOUR.  Gate-wiring is [[ubsanshiftlane]], deliberately 
separate.\n\n*** THE SIBLING QUESTION IS ANSWERED BEFORE THE PANEL ANSWERS IT, AND THE RESULT IS A CLEAN\nABSENCE -- 
RECORDED WITH ITS WARRANT SO IT IS FALSIFIABLE. ***\n\n`#511`'s own pass-2 brief asks (Q5) whether a sibling of this 
shape was missed.  Censused:\n\n    signed-constant  <<  VARIABLE, tree-wide                       317 sites\n    of 
those, literal > 1 AND headroom <= 24                          2 sites\n\n**317 IS A CORRELATE, NOT THE CLASS.**  `1 
<< x` with 31 places of headroom is the ordinary bitmask\nidiom in C and is a defect only if `x` can reach 31.  The 
`#511` SHAPE is distinctive: a literal\nLARGER than 1 (so little headroom) shifted by a variable that a loop can drive 
to the overflow point.\nFiltering on that leaves TWO:\n\n    cpu_mips_coproc.c:772   tmp &= 0x0fff << PAGEMASK_SHIFT;  
  headroom 20\n    cpu_mips_coproc.c:774   tmp &= 0xffff << PAGEMASK_SHIFT;    headroom 16\n\n**BOTH ARE SAFE, and the 
warrant is a compile-time constant:**\n\n    src/include/cop0.h:85    #define PAGEMASK_SHIFT   13\n    0x0fff << 13 = 
0x01ffe000       0xffff << 13 = 0x1fffe000       INT_MAX = 0x7fffffff\n\n`PAGEMASK_SHIFT` is a MACRO, not a runtime 
variable, so the compiler folds the whole expression and\nthere is no shift to overflow.  **My regex matched an 
identifier and could not tell a macro from a\nvariable** -- which is why the two hits needed reading rather than 
counting.\n\n> **[THIS ABSENCE RECORD IS FALSE.  See the correction at the end of this note -- the grok pass-2\n> seat 
found TWO siblings my filter had hidden.]**  ~~no other site in the tree has a signed literal > 1 shifted by a value 
that can reach 2^31.~~  THE WARRANT IS\n> `PAGEMASK_SHIFT == 13` AND ITS BEING A COMPILE-TIME CONSTANT.**  If either 
changes -- the value\n> raised past 15, or the macro replaced by a variable -- the two `cpu_mips_coproc.c` sites 
become\n> live and this record expires.\n\n*A near-miss worth keeping: my first attempt grepped `define 
PAGEMASK_SHIFT` in `src/` and returned\nNOTHING, and I had already computed the arithmetic assuming 13.  Zero hits is 
not evidence, and the\nnumber I was about to rely on was a guess.  It IS 13 -- found in `src/include/cop0.h` on a 
broader\nsearch -- but the conclusion was reached before the fact was.*\n\n*** THE ABSENCE RECORD ABOVE IS FALSE, AND 
MY OWN FILTER IS WHAT MADE IT SO.  The grok pass-2 seat\nfound TWO SIBLINGS, both verified here. ***\n\ngrok's verdict 
on `#511` closes with: *\"Two other PCI IDSEL scanners still evaluate `1 << 31`.\"*\nVerified by reading:\n\n    
dev_uninorth.c:70   for (dev=11; dev<32; dev++)\n                 :71       if (idata & (1 << dev))            <- dev 
REACHES 31\n    dev_v3.c:164        for (dev=24; dev<32; dev++)\n            :165           if (relative_addr & (1 << 
dev))    <- dev REACHES 31\n\n    1 << 31 = 0x80000000 = 2147483648    INT_MAX = 2147483647    OVERFLOWS\n\n**Both are 
the IDENTICAL SHAPE to `#511`** -- a signed literal shifted by a loop variable the loop\nbound drives to the overflow 
point -- and both loops explicitly run to `dev < 32`, so 31 is reached\nwhenever no earlier bit matches.\n\n*** THE 
FILTER THAT HID THEM WAS MINE, AND IT WAS EXACTLY BACKWARDS. ***  My census excluded\n`if v <= 1: continue`, reasoning 
that ``1 << x`` is the ordinary bitmask idiom in C and only a\ndefect if `x` reaches 31.  **That reasoning is right 
and the exclusion is wrong**: `1` has the MOST\nheadroom (31 places), which makes it the ONLY literal that overflows 
at the maximum shift a\n`< 32` loop can produce.  I filtered on \"little headroom = suspicious\" and thereby removed 
the\nsingle literal whose headroom exactly matches the commonest loop bound in the tree.\n\n> **AN ABSENCE RECORD IS 
ONLY AS GOOD AS THE FILTER THAT PRODUCED IT, AND MY WARRANT NAMED THE\n> WRONG THING.**  I recorded the warrant as 
`PAGEMASK_SHIFT == 13` -- a fact about the two sites the\n> filter DID surface -- when the load-bearing assumption was 
the FILTER ITSELF.  A warrant should\n> name what would falsify the record, and what falsified it was the exclusion, 
not the constant.\n\n**The `PAGEMASK_SHIFT` half stands**: those two `cpu_mips_coproc.c` sites really are safe, for 
the\nreason given.  What is retracted is the universal claim that nothing else in the tree has the shape.\n\n*Filed to 
[[shiftubcensus]], which is the row for this class and was already marked HONESTLY\nPARTIAL.  Recorded here too 
because THIS row is where the false absence was written.*\n\n*** codex, `#511` PASS 2, CHALLENGES THE \"GRACEFUL 
DEGRADATION PRECEDENT\" THAT BOTH LCA ROWS LEAN\nON. ***\n\n*\"`DEVICE_ACCESS(lca_pci_conf)`'s fallback selects device 
zero and forwards the access through\n`bus_pci_setaddr`.  **That is an ALIASING DECISION, not by itself proof of 
harmless degradation.**\nThe comment's 'transferable warrant' needs its own justification; the shift repair does not 
establish\nit.\"*\n\nThe `dev >= 21` arm -- commented-out `fatal()`/`exit(1)` with `dev = 0;` substituted -- has 
been\ncited repeatedly here, including by [[lcabadval]], as the file's own in-tree warrant for deleting a\nhost kill.  
**codex's point is that substituting device ZERO is not a decline: it silently redirects\nthe access to a DIFFERENT 
DEVICE.**  Whether that is harmless is a separate question nobody has\nasked, and \"someone already did it in this 
file\" is not the same as \"it is right\".\n\n> **A TRANSFERRED WARRANT NEEDS ITS OWN JUSTIFICATION, NOT JUST A 
PRECEDENT.**  This is the\n> option-set rule's own caution turned around: grepping the fork for an existing idiom 
finds what the\n> tree DOES, which is evidence about practice and not about correctness.\n\n*Not resolved here.  
Recorded on both rows because both cite it, and any round that leans on it owes\nthe justification codex is asking 
for.*  #511, commit c7d7414 (NOT 7a41b3f).  `0x800 << dev' -> `0x800U << dev' -- VERIFIED LIVE AT HEAD.  The witness 
is NOT a new probe: it is the existing lca_confbus_probe run against the ASAN/UBSAN build; build/ stayed 3/4 with `bus 
kill' still red, which is the control that the differential measured the UB and not something else.  PASS 2 IS ON DISK 
(artifacts/lcashiftub/pass2_c7d7414/, six seats): FOUR SEATS REFUSED the `tag is already a wider unsigned' reason -- 
the TOKEN was ratified and the REASON corrected in the product comment, which is the advice-survives-its-reason shape. 
 Detector is a UBSAN differential and is EXPLICITLY NOT gate-wired (`ubsanshiftlane`); sibling `1 << 31` scanners in 
dev_uninorth.c and dev_v3.c are filed to `shiftubcensus`.  LOW is right: language UB, no measured wrong guest value, 
intended codegen on this compiler. CLOSED 2026-09-17 on the grok triage (regress/artifacts/<row>/ and 
