files it as a dead seat.  It is not: the seat is healthy and will answer the SAME QUESTION reworded.  Reporting it as 
a wall would lose an available seat, which is the sixth seat-failure class in a new coat.\n\nPRACTICE, not machinery: 
write panel briefs in the vocabulary of the ENGINEERING TASK.  This project's briefs are about bounds correctness, 
error handling and detector coverage, and they read better in those words anyway -- the re-routed #519 brief was 
CLEARER than the one that was refused.  No checker is proposed: there is no mechanical test for 'this phrasing will be 
flagged', and a checker that guessed would fire on honest briefs, which is how a check gets switched off."
