>      "ev": "regress/artifacts/ip30abortkill/EXITHUNT_grok_20260917.txt; src/devices/dev_mvme187.c:63-68,127-129; 
src/include/thirdparty/mvme_memcreg.h:31-; src/machines/machine_mvme88k.c:88",
       "note": "`dev_mvme187.c:68` indexes a 124-byte struct with a guest-supplied offset of up to 255, **BEFORE the 
switch and unconditionally on every access including reads**:  `odata = ((uint8_t*)&d->memcreg)[relative_addr];`  The 
device is registered with length **0x200** at `:127-129`, and `:63-66` folds the high half down (`if (relative_addr & 
0x100) { controller = 1; relative_addr &= ~0x100; }`), so the index domain is 0..255.  **sizeof(struct memcreg) is 
124** -- DERIVED LOCALLY by counting the 62 `volatile u_char` declarations in `src/include/thirdparty/mvme_memcreg.h` 
(31 registers, each followed by a 3-byte `xxN[3]` pad), which independently reproduces the hunting seat's figure.  
**So offsets 124..255 are a 132-byte host OUT-OF-BOUNDS READ past the struct**, into whatever follows it inside the 
malloc'd `struct mvme187_data`. REACHABILITY: `machine_mvme88k.c:88` `device_add(machine, \"mvme187\")` -- note this 
is `machine_mvme88k.c`, NOT `machine_m88k.c`, which the hunting seat named loosely and where my first grep found 
nothing; I corrected it by locating the constructor rather than by trusting the citation. *** THE REASON THIS IS A 
RIDER AND NOT A SECOND KILL: the `default:` arm already `exit(1)`s, so TODAY THE OOB VALUE NEVER ESCAPES TO THE GUEST 
-- the read happens, the process dies, and the kill is already inside `exitunowned76`. ***  **The exposure is what a 
DE-FATALISATION of that arm would create**, and it is the `asicindexcase` shape exactly: the `exit(1)` is doing duty 
as the bounds check, so removing the kill without clamping the index converts a host death into a SILENT heap 
over-read served to the guest as register data.  A round that de-fatalises this file owes the clamp IN THE SAME DIFF 
-- a bound, not a `case`.  Filed MED so it is queued BEFORE the de-fatalisation round rather than discovered inside 
it."
      }
