     "commits": [],
     "opened": "2026-09-17",
     "title": "census of probes that could report `alive' for a process that already died -- 0 shipped live probes 
mis-score; the class was born and closed the same day",
>    "state_note": "*** CENSUSED 2026-09-17 AND THE CLASS IS CLOSED WITH ITS DENOMINATOR: **0 shipped live probes 
still mis-score this way.**  The defect was born today and died today. ***  The founding case is 
`regress/artifacts/ip30abortkill/ip30_abort_probe.py`, which had the exact shape, was MEASURED reporting `alive` for a 
process that had SIGABRT'd, and was rewritten to poll the same hour.  `arm_msrmode_probe.py` was built with the 
polling form from the start. **METHOD, keyed on MECHANISM rather than on names** -- and it explicitly refused to count 
`artifacts/**` frozen copies, which would have inflated the class about FIFTEENFOLD by re-counting the same five 
files: live population is `regress/*.py` = **99 files**, minus 10 harness/selftest/census scripts and one source-only 
probe = **88 launchers**. **THE DEATH-AS-ORACLE FAMILIES, with counts:** EOF-as-alive (`alive = rd(...)`) **33**; 
sessions borrowed from those 33 **11** (pcc2_default execs pcc2_width's session; ten SH4 probes import 
sh4_pcic_probe); prompt/dump still-answering **3**; `subprocess.run` wait-status **6**; **`WNOHANG` at all: 5** (4 at 
HEAD plus the uncommitted arm_msrmode). **OF THOSE FIVE, HOW MANY SAMPLE waitpid ONCE?**  `pcc2_width_probe.py` polls 
30x0.1s and waitpid only fills `how`; `pcc2_c040_probe.py` the same; `xscale_inten_probe.py` polls 2s in `close()` and 
sets `self.dead` on EOF during `send()`; `arm_msrmode_probe.py` polls 12s. `luna_absentcpu_probe.py` **does sample 
once -- and it is NOT the alive oracle**, being called from `died()` only after `step_at` has already failed on EOF.  
**ONCE-ONLY IN THE LIVE TREE: 1.  WAITPID-ONCE AS THE SURVIVE ORACLE: 0.** *** AND THE SEAT NAMED THE CONSTRUCTION 
RATHER THAN THE KEYWORD, which is what makes this reusable: the bug is NOT 'has WNOHANG'.  It is the three-part 
combination -- `rd()` returns on an empty `os.read` so the spin is skipped exactly on death; that return is IGNORED; 
and `alive` is then taken from a single `waitpid(WNOHANG)`.  Any one of the three alone is harmless. ***  
**DISPOSITION: NO TREE-WIDE EDIT.**  The seat's own words -- *'a tree-wide rewrite would manufacture findings'* -- and 
this project's addition licence agree: 33 EOF-as-alive probes consume `rd()`'s return and are correct as written.  The 
boundary is recorded so a future round does not rediscover the class and sweep it.",
