     "title": "eleven probe exemptions in check_probe_wiring.py all expire 2026-09-20 -- a deliberate alignment of TWO 
debts that nine later exemptions copied, so the checker reds on eleven unrelated probes at once",
>    "state_note": "*** STATUS 2026-09-25 (GXEMUL): #550 DISPERSES the block -- ten dates, 2026-10-08 to 2026-12-03, 
each with its reason (regress/artifacts/exemptredate_20260925/).  CLOSED. ***\n\n*** STATUS 2026-09-18 (GXEMUL): #536 
SHIPS under `wiringcliff`.  Two probes wired (mk48_nvram, hpcmips_ctor); the other ELEVEN re-dated to 2026-09-27 BY 
OWNER RULING -- one block again, valid on the 27th, RED from 2026-09-28.  That is the cliff this row names, re-created 
on purpose; the row stays open until it is dispersed or discharged. ***\n\n*** ELEVEN PROBE EXEMPTIONS FALL DUE ON THE 
SAME DAY, 2026-09-20 -- THREE DAYS FROM THIS FILING.  Measured 2026-09-17 by the Opus 5 seat and verified here. ***  A 
date histogram over `check_probe_wiring.py`'s `EXEMPT` table: **11 entries dated `2026-09-20`**, plus one `2026-09-19` 
and one `2026-09-21` -- so **thirteen exemptions expire inside three days**, eleven of them together. *** AND THE 
PILE-UP IS AN ACCIDENT OF A DELIBERATE CHOICE, WHICH IS THE PART WORTH RECORDING. ***  The file's own comment explains 
the date: *\"2026-09-20 matches the fbpending_bound:2026-09-20 deadline already standing in gate_offline.sh's 
SM_EXEMPT, so `#442`'s two debts fall due together.\"*  **Aligning TWO debts was a good idea; nine more have since 
been written to the same date, and nobody chose that.**  Each new exemption copied the date it found. **WHAT IT COSTS 
IF NOTHING IS DONE:** on 2026-09-20 the checker reds on eleven probes at once, and a gate that reds on eleven 
unrelated things is the shape this project already names -- *a rule that retro-fails at scale gets switched off, and a 
disabled rule is worse than no rule*.  The honest options are to WIRE them, to RE-DATE them individually with their 
own warrants, or to retire the ones whose rounds are closed -- but **not** to push the whole table forward as one 
edit, which is how the pile-up formed. *Note one of the eleven is `ppc_rldicl_probe.py`, whose repair is uncommitted 
and whose row (`ppcwitnessmaskoracle`) is open -- so that debt is about to come due on an oracle nothing executes.*",
