121: *** THE ATTRIBUTION RULE, WITHOUT WHICH HALF THESE ROWS ARE VACUOUS AND LOOK FINE: ***
122: All FIVE ISR sites print ONE IDENTICAL STRING behind ONE SHARED BIT.  So a row can attribute an
123: announce to a SPECIFIC arm ONLY IF its session makes a SINGLE ISR access.  A multi-access
124: session asserts merely "at least one of these arms announced" -- which is exactly how the
