                        "note":  "*** THE TICK ROW IS BUILDABLE AND IS MEASURED: `step 1\u0027 KILLS THE HOST.  The codex/agy split is settled BY MEASUREMENT, and BOTH SEATS WERE HALF RIGHT WHILE THE DECISIVE FACT WAS NAMED BY NEITHER. ***  codex was right that stepping alone is insufficient -- the guard must be ARMED (measured: no store + 70000 steps -\u003e alive; bit 49 + 70000 steps -\u003e alive).  agy was right that free-run is NOT needed, but its stated reason -- a 65536-cycle period implying `step 70000\u0027 -- is not why the cheap row works.  **THE MECHANISM, verified by me in the source and not taken from the seat:** `machine_add_tickfunction\u0027 sets `ticks_till_next[n] = 0\u0027 (`machine.c:354\u0027) while `ticks_reset_value[n] = 1 \u003c\u003c tickshift\u0027 (`:355\u0027), and `machine_run()\u0027 decrements then fires while `\u003c= 0\u0027 (`:727\u0027).  **So the FIRST `machine_run()\u0027 of any session drives it to -1 and fires EVERY tick function immediately** -- `step 1\u0027 executes the store and then runs the tick in that same `machine_run()\u0027.  *** A THIRD FACT NEITHER SEAT NAMED, AND IT IS A FALSE-GREEN TRAP I WOULD HAVE WALKED INTO: **BIT 50 CANNOT BE SET BY `sw\u0027.** ***  `case 0x10000\u0027 does `d-\u003eimask0 = idata\u0027 with `idata = memory_readmax64(cpu, data, len)\u0027, so a FOUR-BYTE store caps idata below 2^32 -- measured, `sw 0xffffffff\u0027 + 70000 steps -\u003e ALIVE.  Arming requires **`sd\u0027 = 0xFCE80000** (readback `ld\u0027 = 0xDC220000).  **`OP_SW_T0_A3\u0027 IS THE ONLY STORE HELPER IN `ip30_abort_probe.py\u0027**, so a tick row copy-pasted from it would arm nothing, stay alive, and SCORE GREEN ON A LIVE HOST DEATH.  **PERIODICITY IS NOT A STARTUP ARTIFACT** -- the boundary was measured from TWO different warm offsets, both sides: warm=10 gives alive at N=65525 and DEAD at 65526; warm=100 gives alive at 65435 and DEAD at 65436.  Both put tick #2 at `machine_run\u0027 #65536 exactly, so ticks fire at MR #