                        "ev":  "Fable adjudication 2026-09-17; gate_asan_sweep.sh:593; dev_sgi_ip32.c vs dev_sgi_ip30.c INTERRUPT_* counts",
                        "note":  "*** FABLE 5.1 ADJUDICATION, 2026-09-17.  IDENTITY VERIFIED -- `claude-fable-5-1`, the nonce, AND the verbatim first line of CHECKPOINT.md, so prompt delivery and file access are proven rather than assumed.  Fired LAST, after all 8 scriptable transports and the Opus measurement. *** **SHIP ORDER: (c) commit the reviewed working set -\u003e (b) run `arm_msrmode_probe.py` -\u003e (a) the ip30 fix as its OWN round.**  Serialisation note it supplied and I had not: (b) runs the emulator and (c) runs a gate, and they contend on CPU but NOT on the tree -- so run (b) to completion, THEN (c)\u0027s gate alone. **A2 -- Q3 IS ALREADY ANSWERED AND THE FIX DOES NOT WAIT.**  DECLINE the read at 0x10020; do not mirror `d-\u003eisr`, do not return 0-as-a-value.  *** AND IT RULED ON A SECOND DISPOSITION MY FIVE QUESTIONS NEVER REACHED: DECLINE THE 0x10030 **WRITE** ARM TOO. ***  heart.h documents `isr` as read-only and the fork\u0027s clear-on-write is a member-6 BACKED ACCEPT standing without a warrant, which the addition licence does not permit -- Linux/IP30 clears via 0x10028, which the file already implements.  Same function, same case labels, same detector family, so same round.  It owes a STATE row (write declined AND `isr` unchanged), not merely an `alive\u0027 row. **A3 -- MY FRAMING WAS WRONG AND THE CORRECTION IS THE USEFUL PART.**  These are not four defects competing to join a round under the reopening rule.  **They are ONE ABANDONED FEATURE** -- the identical `fatal(\"IP30 legacy interrupt rewrite: TODO\"); abort();` at every reachable exit of a rewrite nobody finished.  The unit of work is the FEATURE, not the site, and splitting it would de-fatalise three of four exits and leave the fourth a live host death, which is the de-escalation clause\u0027s own hazard.  *** AND IT REFUSED TO LET ME GLOSS THE COST: the \u0027no new oracle\u0027 criterion IS genuinely violated -- the tick needs its own periodicity oracle and its own latch bit, so THE ROUND SHIPS TWO DETECTORS, and the round record must NAME that deviation rather than let a two-probe structure read as an accident. *** **A4 -- IT FOUND MY WEAKEST CORRECTION AND IT IS RIGHT.**  My (iv) said the `acc imask\u0027 row is safe *because it writes bit 18 AND because `sw\u0027 cannot set bit 50*.  Both clauses are true and **clause (2) MISDIRECTS**: the row\u0027s value `1\u003c\u003c18` has no high bits at any width, so width is irrelevant to THIS row -- while \u0027sw cannot set bit 50\u0027 reads as a general safety invariant for imask0, and **the death IS reachable, by `sd 1\u003c\u003c50`**.  *** MY OWN PROBE\u0027S COMMENT IS STRONGER AND MORE HONEST THAN MY SUMMARY OF IT: it calls that row a documented HAZARD and warns that copy-pasting it as a kill row would \u0027arm NOTHING, stay ALIVE, and score green on a live host death\u0027.  My correction re-labelled a HAZARD as a SAFETY PROPERTY. ***  That is the a-correction-is-not-safer-than-what-it-corrects rule landing on me. **A4(i) -- MY WARRANT OVERCLAIMED TRANSFERABILITY, verified locally:** `dev_sgi_ip32.c` has 6 INTERRUPT_CONNECT/ASSERT sites; **`dev_sgi_ip30.c` has ZERO, and zero `struct interrupt` members.**  \u0027CRIME uses it\u0027 proves the IDIOM exists on MIPS; it does not prove member 7 is BUILDABLE for ip30, which has no interrupt topology at all.  The correct statement is *member 7\u0027s idiom is available; its application to ip30 requires building the HEART topology and is substantial* -- which is the carrier\u0027s own 2026-09-06 lesson (check the member is available on THIS CPU; a precedent real elsewhere is not thereby transferable). **A5 -- THE QUESTION I WAS NOT ASKING, AND IT IS THE RIGHT ONE: DOES `ip30abortkill` ACTUALLY OUTRANK `armmsrmodekill`?**  Rung is a FLOOR ON ADMISSIBILITY; SEVERITY orders the queue, and severity rests on real-guest reachability **that is measured for NEITHER**.  Verified locally: `gate_asan_sweep.sh:593` runs `for s in ip12 ip28 ip30 ip32 ip35` and is GREEN, so **the ISR aborts are on no path anything in-tree travels today**; only one gate names ip30 at all, and the device\u0027s own header says it is \u0027just comprised of hardcoded guesses so far.\u0027  Meanwhile `armmsrmodekill` kills the PROCESS on ARM, whose decode IS exercised across testarm/barearm/cats.  **So the order between the two HIGHs was set without the measurement that would settle it** -- which is itself the argument for running the arm probe BEFORE the larger ip30 build: the cheap measurement informs the order of the expensive work."
