                        "note":  "*** DO NOT SHIP AS-IS -- THE FIX IS RIGHT, THE DETECTOR IS NOT.  SIX INDEPENDENT CLEAN-SWEEP MUTANTS AT 19/19 against the then-shipped 19-row instrument, zero rows red. ***  The measuring seat, in a scratch clone, baseline NAMED and frozen, rebuilt with [binary -nt source] verified before mutant 1, clone-local sentinel, restore from the named baseline.  Every table verified by its IP30ABORT_DONE sentinel; all 33 artifacts PRESERVED BY THE MAIN LOOP to regress/artifacts/ip30abortkill/opus_killtable_20260917/ because the seat is read-only and could not write a durable path itself.  THE SIX ESCAPES: M9_silent20wr (drop the 0x10020 WRITE announce) 19/19; M5_silent28wr (same at 0x10028) 19/19; M1_silent30 (same at 0x10030) 19/19; M3_sharedbit (IP30_W_ISR (1\u003c\u003c1)-\u003e(1\u003c\u003c0), ONE CHARACTER) 19/19; M2_nolatch ((1\u003c\u003c1)-\u003e(0\u003c\u003c1), latch defeated, unbounded flood) 19/19; M8_noclr28 (delete d-\u003eisr \u0026= ~idata) 19/19.  *** THE LOAD-BEARING ONE: M1_silent30 IS `M_latch_silent_30\u0027, THE MUTANT `kill 30 txt\u0027\u0027s OWN COMMENT CLAIMS TO CLOSE -- and the row was green under it. ***  The seat gave the mechanism the main loop had only half seen: the row read a different session, AND because all five ISR sites print ONE identical string behind ONE shared bit, `kill 30 txt\u0027 attributes to NO SINGLE ARM AT ALL -- it asserts only \u0027at least one of three ISR accesses announced\u0027.  So M9 escapes for the same reason even after the re-binding: only a SINGLE-ACCESS session can attribute an announce.  *** THE NEGATIVE CONTROL PASSES, WHICH IS WHAT MAKES THE REST CREDIBLE: M4_silenttick scored 18/19 with `tick 50 txt\u0027 RED. ***  The codex seat found that cell by reading, the main loop\u0027s repair landed at 22:07, and the seat measured it FAILABLE -- and separately confirmed on the 18-row instrument that the escape had been real before it.  AND THE MAIN LOOP\u0027S OWN TABLE, RUNNING CONCURRENTLY, CONFIRMS THE REPAIR DIRECTION: M1_del28store (= this seat\u0027s M8_noclr28, its severest escape) scores 20/21 with `isr clr\u0027 RED against the 21-row instrument.  The row four packet-fed seats converged on KILLS the escape the measuring seat found.  FINDINGS BEYOND THE TABLE, each checkable: (1) PREMISE 1 IS TRUE OF HEAD AND FALSE OF WHAT SHIPS -- \"according to Linux/IP30\" appears 3x pre-fix and 1x post-fix, because the diff rewrites two of the three, and the CHANGELOG repeats the claim.  A present-tense warrant falsified by its own diff.  (2) A STRONGER WARRANT THAN heart.h FOR THE 0x10030 QUESTION, and the brief did not give it: pre-fix the clear was followed UNCONDITIONALLY by abort(), there is no SIGABRT handler in src/, and the round\u0027s own measurement records KILLED BY SIGNAL 6 -- so no guest ever executed another instruction after that clear and its effect was UNOBSERVABLE BY CONSTRUCTION.  That survives even if heart.h is a driver author\u0027s model rather than a hardware contract, which the round\u0027s own honest-limit section concedes.  (3) THE MEMBER LABEL IS WRONG: 0x10020-WRITE is recorded as member 4 ACCEPT, whose defining property is NO LATCH -- and the shipped code keeps the store AND announces \"rewrite not implemented\" at a site where the rewrite IS implemented (`isr keep\u0027 proves it round-trips).  The announce is warranted (the cpu_interrupt recalculation really is missing) but should say what is missing, not that the rewrite was dropped.  dev_pcc2.c is the in-tree wording model.  (4) TWO LATCH BITS COST INFORMATION, measured: a real driver writes set_isr constantly, the first benign fully-serviced write consumes the bit, and the architecturally-wrong 0x10030 write -- the access this round is most careful about -- is then SILENT FOREVER.  dev_pcc2.c already does the other thing: per-site bits with the site interpolated into the message and an unqualified (once).  Either choice is defensible; NEITHER BEING ROWED is not.  (5) build-asan/ AND /tmp/gxsec-build BOTH FAIL part 2, measured independently of the main loop\u0027s own finding minutes earlier -- and the seat adds the arc tree, which the main loop had recorded as UNCHECKED.  Both cmp clean and carry no sentinel: the documented stale trap.  The 22:08 edit was comment-only (verified by a comment-stripped diff), so nothing measured today is wrong.  (6) THE PROBE CLAIMS 12/12 FOR SIX NAMED MUTANTS WITH NO ARTIFACT NAMED AND NONE ON DISK -- and M_latch_silent_30 is one of them and ESCAPES, so the claim is not merely uncited but REFUTED.  (7) grok\u0027s design pass prescribed SIX closing rows; items 3 and 6 shipped and 1, 2, 4 and 5 did not -- and they are precisely M8, M1, M9/M5 and the mirror mutant.  That is #490\u0027s prescribed-rows-lost-in-a-rewrite pattern, with no PRETABLE.out to diff the new list against.  (PRETABLE.out now EXISTS, written 22:58 -- after this seat began, so its observation was true when made and is time-indexed.)  DENOMINATOR, stated by the seat: SWEPT = announce presence at 4 of 6 sites, the latch predicate weakened two ways, and the guarded body\u0027s own effect at 0x10028.  REASONED ONLY = the two READ announces, the 0x10020 store, writeflag conjunctions, grok\u0027s mirror mutant.  NOT SWEPT AT ALL = the width/len axis (#499\u0027s axis, unexplored here) and position/translation (clause (f)).  CONTENTION CAVEAT in the conservative direction: the main loop ran probes concurrently during part of the table; load makes rows FAIL, not pass, so the clean sweeps are if anything understated.  AND IT APPROVED THE FIX: live abort() 4-\u003e0 (the one remaining match is inside a comment), exit( 0-\u003e0, return 6-\u003e6, every arm breaks so the common tail still runs.  Every behavioural delta strictly an improvement.  *** THE FIX SHIPS UNCHANGED; THE DETECTOR OWES A CLASS CLOSURE. ***"
